the introduction to bioinformatics  course is an introduction to the field  of bioinformatics or the intersection of  informatics and biology it speaks about  the opportunities that come with the  available big data and methods for its  analysis in research and industry  including healthcare agriculture  environmental sciences public health and  more biology is rapidly acquiring the  character of a data science billions of  data points on genes proteins and other  molecules are compiled in large files  and systematically studied analyzing  this data will lead to more knowledge  and understanding about living organisms  including human health  biotechnology crops and livestock  production this course will give an  overview of bioinformatics for students  biologists and clinicians the influx of  data associated methodologies and data  driven research makes bioinformatics for  Life Sciences as prominent as the  emergence of computers for the tech  industry this course is divided into  three sections  introduction to big data bioinformatics  bioinformatics in healthcare and  translational bioinformatics all of  these sections can be completed in under  two hours of study the course will  provide important information  terminology and perspectives from  experts on this exciting field there are  three sections and a quiz at the end the  course can be taken by anyone without  any special prior knowledge in related  fields after signing up and completing  the profile you will be able to see your  progress and notice points accumulating  under your profile based on this  activity you can see how you master  important skills and acquire  certificates of completion for this  course and other ones that you will find  on the edu that t - bio data info  platform as an introductory course you  will also learn about a project-based  approach to learning bioinformatics we  take datasets from high impact  publications and convert them into  online learning experiences each  subsequent course you will take will  have a practical application that  demonstrates  how bioinformatics can be used these  projects will fall under certain  specializations like oncology  neuroscience agro tech and others the  specializations provide domain expertise  and explain basic bioinformatics  concepts related to that subject as a  result anyone starting on this journey  in bioinformatics can start developing a  project of their own by seeing how  experts analyze their data and achieve  research results you can start  developing a research question of your  own identify the appropriate type of  data and planning your analysis this  introductory course leads into multiple  courses and projects that can serve as a  springboard into the world of  bioinformatics in subsequent courses we  will be utilizing the T bio info  platform to process big datasets this  platform is built for multi-omics  integration and analysis of structured  data with advanced methods like machine  learning and mathematical modeling after  you set up your account make sure to try  out the analytical platform you can do  so by filling out a form on server dot t  - bio that info the analytical platform  will provide hands-on experience for  anyone to apply to learn skills -  interesting datasets with color coded  logical maps explanation of methods  detailed input and output formats and  reproducible workflows this course  provides a broad overview but it is  structured to offer significant depth  even for the experienced users after  completing this short introduction you  will be inspired to continue learning  about the exciting field of  bioinformatics this program has been  tested in multiple universities around  the world and reviewed by experts in the  field of bioinformatics we are excited  that you joined so let's start learning
 

